codemap 9
tour feature-server-status
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human, opening a repo in the window and reaching for hover, go-to or references, needs to know which language servers answer for it, which are still starting or indexing, and which are missing: a missing server means its files get no hover or go-to and keep tree-sitter's calls, which reads as a broken feature unless the server is named. Goal: understanding a codebase through codemap takes less friction than through an editor with an LSP. The owner listed it in TODO.md (GUI 5: with several language servers missing, the status line names only one; Features 2: a status dot per language server). Seen in a run of the build without it, on a project of one Rust, one Python and one JavaScript file with only rust-analyzer on PATH (a script of dump, idle, wait 5, dump): the status line read 'typescript-language-server: starting', then 'typescript-language-server not on PATH: its files keep the tree-sitter resolver, no hover or go-to for them'; pyright-langserver, also missing, was never named, and rust-analyzer, which answered, was not shown at all. Whichever failure arrived last won the line, so the GUI scripts clicked save before their first dump only to overwrite it. Nothing else in codemap shows it: the backend progress label names one server only while a batch runs, and the CLI's notices go to stderr of a CLI run. The status bar holds one item per language of the index, in Language order (Rust, Odin, C, Python, JavaScript), sized to its text and grouped at the right before the map's directory: a dot and the server's program, green when ready, orange while starting or indexing, red when missing or failed to start, dim when nothing has asked it yet (a repo whose files are all cached starts no server until a hover). The status line keeps the index count and the outcome of what the reader did, so after the servers settle it reads the same on every run. The same project in this build: right after launch rust-analyzer is orange and the other two red ('DUMP servers rust-analyzer=starting pyright-langserver=missing typescript-language-server=missing'), and once idle rust-analyzer is green ('rust-analyzer=ready'). The owner asked for one design, the dots of the TODO item, so no alternatives were built.

